  ans:0, expl:"The correct choice is &ldquo;Losses on a short are theoretically unlimited (price can rise without bound), while gains are capped (price cannot fall below zero)&rdquo;. Review Chapter 6 &mdash; Secondary Market Transaction Support Operations &mdash; for the underlying concept.",
